{
  "program": "CBTRN03C",
  "caseId": "case02",
  "description": "The page boundary, at exactly twenty lines. WS-PAGE-SIZE is PIC 9(03) COMP-3 VALUE 20 (:131) and WS-LINE-COUNTER is PIC 9(09) COMP-3 (:129); the first-time header write advances the counter by four before any detail line, so MOD(WS-LINE-COUNTER, WS-PAGE-SIZE) = 0 first holds at the SEVENTEENTH record, where the counter reads 20. That record therefore emits 1110-WRITE-PAGE-TOTALS and a fresh 1120-WRITE-HEADERS BEFORE its own detail line, which is the ordering emergent from the two IFs at :275 and :282 running in that order. Seventeen equal amounts make the boundary the only thing that can move the output.",
